---
# Multi-repo registry. One Symphony worker can dispatch into any entry below,
# routing per-issue via a `repo:<name>` Linear label.
#
# Routing rules (see apps/worker/src/config/repos.ts):
#   1. First `repo:<name>` label on the issue picks the matching entry.
#   2. Issues with no `repo:*` label are silently ineligible — they stay in
#      whatever tracker state they're in and are never dispatched.
#
# Each entry's `env:` is merged into the hook environment AND the agent
# adapter's environment. `${VAR}` is expanded from process.env at load time;
# the hook runner's BLOCKED_ENV (LINEAR_API_KEY etc.) still wins.
#
# To use: copy this file to `repos.md`, edit the entries for your repos, then
# `kill -HUP <worker-pid>` (or restart). `repos.md` is gitignored — your
# operator-specific entries live there, not here.
repos:
  - name: backend-api
    repo_url: https://github.com/your-org/backend-api
    install_cmd: npm ci
    agent_backend: claude

  - name: frontend-app
    repo_url: https://github.com/your-org/frontend-app
    install_cmd: pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
    agent_backend: claude
    env:
      # Per-repo secrets pulled from .env.local via ${VAR} interpolation.
      APP_SESSION_COOKIE: ${APP_SESSION_COOKIE}
---

# Repos

Add a `repo:<name>` label to a Linear issue to route it to that target.
Issues without a `repo:*` label are not picked up.
